{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/touring-exhibition/883","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Of Mythic Worlds: Works from the 16th Century to Today","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"The Drawing Center","id":"actor/2072","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"Of Mythic Worlds will focus on shared commonalities within spirituality, ritual, and myth across different cultures, geography, and time, drawing parallels between works as a way of highlighting these intersections. Spanning four centuries, the 46 drawings in the show will cross historical periods and cultural traditions, and through this non-linear art historical context, will illustrate how superstitions and metaphysical beliefs can exist simultaneously.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"Activity"}